{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789216541,"nonce":"micWZaWGjW7dsP7jLMQupglsfV4=","title":"A virtual-method closure over a receiver whose class inherits the method indexes the wrong table","message":"OVirtualClosure carries the vtable slot (pindex). The LLVM emitter (calls.rs emit_air_virtual_closure) and the interpreter (ops.rs op_virtual_closure) both used it as a position in the receiver's class's OWN proto list, which holds only the methods that class declares. For class A { f } / class C extends A {} / class D extends C { override f } and (c:C).f: the AOT build panicked 'index out of bounds: the len is 0' at calls.rs, the LLVM tier was blacklisted in hybrid, and the interpreter stored a null closure ('CallClosure on null closure'). Cranelift walked the super chain by pindex, as HashLink's jit.c does, and was right. Haxe emits OVirtualClosure only when an override exists below the receiver's static type, which is why nothing in the suites reached it. Fixture: test_virtual_closure_inherited.hl.","files":null}]}